## Import

You can import an object storage resource using either the CLI method or the [experimental import block](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/import).

**CLI Import**

The `latitudesh_object_storage` resource can be imported by specifying the bucket ID:

```sh
terraform import latitudesh_object_storage.backups <BUCKET_ID>
```

**Import Block (Experimental)**

Terraform v1.5.0 and later supports the experimental import block, which allows you to define imports in your configuration.

```hcl
import {
  to = latitudesh_object_storage.backups
  id = "<BUCKET_ID>"
}
```

Then run:

```sh
terraform plan -generate-config-out=generated_object_storage.tf
```

> **Note:** The import block feature is experimental and its syntax or behavior may change in future Terraform versions.
